  DDR4-2666 single channel: 21.3 GB/s peak (72 bits = 64 data + 8 ECC).
  Measured on this platform (2026-10-13): write ~14.2, read ~14.4-14.6 GB/s (2 ports).
  All DDR traffic -- both kernels AND QDMA -- shares ONE door into the DDRMC,
  so a second port raises reads (~9.4 -> ~14.6) but not writes.
  A low number here is almost always the kernel clock, not the NoC: check it
  with `v80-smi debug clockwiz -d <bdf> --get --region user`. One 512-bit port
  at 100 MHz is 6.4 GB/s and nothing else matters until that is raised.

